That's true; we didn't want it to be something that showed up everywhere,
though: we wanted to build it in a way that meant you a) had to find it and b)
didn't hit you too hard in-game if you accepted it.

Maybe I should explain what we want to do with the new Challenge trophies (we
intend to add a new one every year).

The idea is, like the Most Unique Deaths trophy, to provide some side
entertainment for the players for whom the normal ascension and score based
trophy slots are a distant dream.  (I, personally, have only ascended once, so
wouldn't stand a chance in the tournament).

The Challenges are (will be) written to have a plot connected to NetHack's plot
(as this one, which involves a Wizard of Yendor from an alternate dimension)
and may take place outside NetHack, though accepting one may also limit the
options you have in the game in some way.

Since I hadn't realized how important Elbereth was to some folks, and don't
really want to change the Challenge at this point, I will add an option to
revoke the challenge on the player home page (it's pretty simple to do this,
from the programming side).  Revoking it will be permanent, though: once you
tell the system to ignore a challenge, there's no way to re-activate it.

On the plus side, though, it'll still be available next year (along with
whatever the new challenge is) so even if you ignore it this year you can try
it then.

I hope that made sense,
-robin



